<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Miracles of Saint Demetrius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Miracles of Saint Demetrius is a Byzantine Greek collection of stories about the patron saint of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessalonica</a>, compiled in two main books in the 7th century. It describes the sieges of the city by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> and names Slavic groups such as the Drougoubitai, Strymonians and Belegezites. It is one of the main sources for the Slavic settlement of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/miracles-of-saint-demetrius.jpg" alt="Miracles of Saint Demetrius" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: From the middle ages unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ActaSanctiDemetrii292.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
